  "releaseNotes": "Version 3.4.1 - Fixes a blank white window on machines that never had the .NET SDK. blazor.web.js and cheap-blazor-interop.js now travel with the app instead of being resolved out of the build machine's NuGet cache: both reach wwwroot as content that survives dotnet publish, and both are embedded in the library assembly as a fallback that cannot go missing. A static web assets manifest pointing at paths that no longer exist no longer kills the process at startup, and the host now checks its own page at startup and logs any script or stylesheet that comes back failing or empty - including the 200-with-zero-bytes case that reports as healthy everywhere else. Previous release: private update feeds via WithVelopackUpdates(repoUrl, accessToken).",
